<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I0e7cae92808d487988a591fcf870c3ef760ecaf9" commit="5a6bc4882fcc1364f27d587e2c84a08e3040005e" commit_message="attestation: implement stubs for ex-cryptohome dbus interface  In certain setups (for now, in tpm2 case), cryptohomed bounces attestation-related messages to attestationd. Define missing messages in dbus interface and implement empty stubs for handling them. The actual implementatons and the corresponding tests will be provided in followup CLs.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:54712 TEST=attestationd starts and cryptohome builds for tpm2,      manually invoking the added methods using      &quot;cryptohome --action&quot; returns appropriate errors.  Change-Id: I0e7cae92808d487988a591fcf870c3ef760ecaf9 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/368963 Commit-Ready: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Darren Krahn &lt;dkrahn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="368963" owner_email="apronin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="10" project="aosp/platform/system/tpm" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/aosp/platform/system/tpm" ref="refs/changes/63/368963/10" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I92cfb13769e5ef46dbbe4e9f645a56d2287fe64a" commit="fddb7b738eebc666995c911f063c4152fe6aef4f" commit_message="cryptohome: implement ServiceDistributed  Add implementation for the option when attestation-related functionality is provided by attestationd service, and cryptohome redirects attestation dbus calls there.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:368963 BUG=chrome-os-partner:54712 TEST=start on tpm2 board, check the log  Change-Id: I92cfb13769e5ef46dbbe4e9f645a56d2287fe64a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/373622 Commit-Ready: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Darren Krahn &lt;dkrahn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="373622" owner_email="apronin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="9" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/22/373622/9" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic361c2cf0904d05b959fad51c53b2fd983b22bc9" commit="67b8939ba29dedba7cc2d8aa85c4c1e1d0553179" commit_message="login: Set cgroup parent directory for android containers  Android will now run in a new cgroup namespace.  This will allow it to modify its own cgroups while not knowing that it is part of a larger cgroup hierarchy.  Configure the external cgroup &quot;session_manager_containers&quot; that will be the root of Android's cgroup namespace.  BUG=b/29259708 TEST=Start android and check that it is in a new cgroup namespace rooted at session_manager_containers.  Change-Id: Ic361c2cf0904d05b959fad51c53b2fd983b22bc9 Signed-off-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/362099 Reviewed-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="9" gerrit_number="362099" owner_email="dgreid@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/99/362099/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="9"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I83e93ea6135f2b3f4baa4816eacacd1e02f1986a" commit="1570bcaf742fe8ac6d82ce493261af9d60260f66" commit_message="libcontainer: Run containers in a cgroup namespace  Now that all of our supported kernels support cgroup namespaces, enable them when running a container.  This will allow the container to modify cgroup parameters for sub groups but still allows the system to control overall limits.  The contained processes will not know that it is in a cgroup namespace, it appears as the root inside the namespace.  BUG=b/29259708 TEST=boot android on cyan and check cgroup membership inside and outside the container.  Change-Id: I83e93ea6135f2b3f4baa4816eacacd1e02f1986a Signed-off-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/362350 " fail_count="7" gerrit_number="362350" owner_email="dgreid@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/50/362350/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="7"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5e88a4b38f357bb08449de302a5c813f572136d2" commit="083d92e0d3b932a0fadf5135456afe01a8a690f1" commit_message="cros_sdk: improve curl output parsing  Derived from CoreOS commit add4c2e24ca7e23bb3895fdea8fa58eab950f9dc https://github.com/coreos/chromite/pull/21      &quot;&quot;&quot;     Blindly searching for '200 OK' doesn't work with HTTP/2 which doesn't     include a text description in the response. Match the status line by     prefix instead. Seems less foolish anyway.     &quot;&quot;&quot;  Might as well future-proof against HTTP revisions up to 9.9 ;)  BUG=chromium:541462 TEST=`cros_sdk`; set up new chroot; trybots  Change-Id: I5e88a4b38f357bb08449de302a5c813f572136d2 Inspired-by: Michael Marineau &lt;michael.marineau@coreos.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/373685 Tested-by: Harry Pan &lt;gs0622@gmail.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="373685" owner_email="briannorris@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/85/373685/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.10" change_id="I407b2f93942e81f2e251afe9669f3f32f161d8fc" commit="519e45858ad68fd0de880103ecbc1ccdbebb4193" commit_message="CHROMIUM: ARM: tegra: add supplies for backlight